{
  "schema": "uibc-core/conformance-vectors@3",
  "generated_by": "tools/conformance_vectors.py",
  "what_this_is": "Inputs and expected bytes for seven steps: canonical JSON, Ed25519 signatures, receipt envelope digests, the linear chain link, Merkle roots and inclusion paths (RFC 6962), policy artefact digests, and two anchor-binding cases against a real RFC 3161 token. It is not a full-receipt corpus and it does not contain a second implementation.",
  "how_to_use": "For each vector, reproduce the expected value with your own implementation: canonical_json - compare bytes and SHA-256; ed25519_signature - verify with any Ed25519 library and compare the verdict; receipt_digest - hash the JCS bytes of the envelope; receipt_chain - recompute the links and compare the verdict; merkle_root - build the RFC 6962 tree and compare the root; merkle_inclusion - recompute the root from the leaf, index, size and path; policy_digest - hash the JCS bytes of the artefact; anchor_binding - hash the artifact and parse the token, then compare the messageImprint. A conforming implementation needs no code from us.",
  "not_claimed": [
    "that we publish a second implementation — we do not",
    "that these vectors validate a receipt schema end to end — they do not; a receipt is a composite of steps that are published here and rules that are not",
    "that passing them makes an implementation interoperable with our receipts — it makes seven steps comparable, not the whole format"
  ],
